      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<p></p>\n\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">[. . . . . . . . .]</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">leads to the deliverance [. . . . . .] what honors them. As for what you mentioned concerning the condition of [. . . . . . . .]</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">and his gratitude from Constantine, for the [. . .] of the farmers has returned(?) and none remain except them. The cause of this\u00a0</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">is therefore not known. He should choose to exercise caution/surround regarding all that belongs to them in the district \u2014 crops/yields, fiscal agents, and other matters \u2014 with the utmost vigilance,</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">and inquire thoroughly into their condition. And if suspicion appears to you, then they have ordered the arrest of Mugh\u0101ra(?) son of [. . .]</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">[and] detention and pressure upon him, he being the one who carries out everything they command; and nothing was accepted from him</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\">] the justice upon them in full and complete measure, and he is not to be granted leniency(?).</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
